5 = 20%</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Q1 2022:
1. 21 districts under IRG region have completed a review of the 2022 district development plan through an intensive one-day workshop inviting government officials such as MOPIC, Ministry of Education, respective districts managers, district core teams, and CSOs among others. The development of gender responsive and inclusive local development plans provides the basis for the local authorities&#x2019; improved capacity to identify community needs, plan and budget implementation. Similarly, in DFA region, 23 initial district development plans have been gathered from five governorates for review and validation.
2. 208 District Core Teams members (59 women, 149 men) have formed across 21 districts in IRG region, with 10 members per each governorate. 
3. No progress yet.
4. Women participants for training activities: 22%; Youth participants: 1%. 
5. No progress yet. The works to support District Authorities with fully functional Womens Affairs Units are underway.

Q2 2022
1. 27 district development plans of 2022 have been developed (21 districts under IRG region; 6 district under DFA region)
2. 44 districts across 9 governorates in Yemen have established District Core Teams (IRG region: 21 districts; DFA region: 23 districts)
3. There is no progress yet
4. Women participants for training activities: 26%; Youth participants: 7%. 
5. The preparatory works have been initiated.

